From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: keep board flow_s recovery exclusive

The upstream RTL8261N/BE link-change callback now schedules an asynchronous
SerDes reset workaround. Boards opting into realtek,patch-rtk-serdes already
use the post-AN flow_s recovery state machine in read_status(). Running both
paths can interleave transactions through the same indirect SerDes window
and reset the block while the board recovery sequence is settling.

Do not schedule the generic reset worker on these opt-in boards. The
property is set once in probe before any link-change callback can run, so
the worker is never queued on this path. Keep its initialization and devm
cancellation intact, and preserve upstream behavior for all other boards.
Do not change the board's register values, pulse delay or carrier retries.

The generic reset workaround originates from Daniel Golle's
7e7c098948cf877d8ebb7e7c17bfdc82a9764f3c, which credits Bo-Cun Chen's
MediaTek SDK workaround. This patch only selects between that unchanged
upstream implementation and the existing downstream board recovery path.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -2577,6 +2577,13 @@
 {
 	struct rtl826x_priv *priv = phydev->priv;
 
+	/* Opt-in boards recover through flow_s in read_status(). Do not race
+	 * that sequence with a reset through the same indirect SerDes window.
+	 * The property is fixed in probe, before this work can ever be queued.
+	 */
+	if (priv->patch_rtk_serdes)
+		return;
+
 	if (phydev->state != PHY_RUNNING) {
 		if (!priv->sds_work_disabled) {
 			disable_delayed_work(&priv->sds_work);
